## 🧪 4. Padrões de Testes Unitários e de Integração com Pest

Todo código gerado pelo Cursor IA DEVE acompanhar seus respectivos testes usando **Pest PHP**.

### Exemplo de Teste Unitário da Máquina de Estados (`tests/Unit/CircuitBreakerStateTest.php`):

```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

use LaravelResilienceKit\CircuitBreaker\Enums\CircuitState;

beforeEach(function () {
    $this->circuit = Resilience::circuitBreaker('test-service')
        ->slidingWindowSize(2)
        ->minimumCalls(2)
        ->failureRateThreshold(100)
        ->recoveryTimeout(10)
        ->halfOpenTrials(2);
});

it('starts in CLOSED state and executes action successfully', function () {
    $result = $this->circuit->run(fn () => 'success');

    expect($result)->toBe('success')
        ->and($this->circuit->getState())->toBe(CircuitState::CLOSED);
});

it('trips to OPEN when failure threshold is reached', function () {
    // Primeira falha
    try {
        $this->circuit->run(fn () => throw new Exception('Service error'));
    } catch (Throwable $e) {}

    expect($this->circuit->getState())->toBe(CircuitState::CLOSED);

    // Segunda falha (atinge threshold = 2)
    try {
        $this->circuit->run(fn () => throw new Exception('Service error'));
    } catch (Throwable $e) {}

    expect($this->circuit->getState())->toBe(CircuitState::OPEN);
});

it('executes fallback when circuit is OPEN', function () {
    // Forçar circuito para OPEN
    $this->circuit->trip();

    $result = $this->circuit
        ->fallback(fn (\Throwable $e) => 'fallback-response')
        ->run(fn () => 'normal-response');

    expect($result)->toBe('fallback-response');
});
```

